{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each of many sites, such as a convention every validation function follows; to use `{impl}` instead when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole; and to mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation of a distributed requirement that its sites do not uphold.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.when` requires the bundled skills to direct agents on three points. Each point is checked by `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_make_a_requirement_distributed_only_for_per_site_obligations]`.\n\nThe test reads the `## Do` section of the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md` through `distributed_reference()` and `section()`. `assert_text` then requires each of two full sentences to appear there.\n\n1. **Distributed only for obligations that apply on their own at each site.** The first sentence is \"Make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each site…\".\n2. **Use `{impl}` when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole.** The first sentence continues \"…when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole, use `{impl}` there.\"\n3. **Mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation the sites do not uphold.** The second sentence is \"Separate obligations each site upholds from obligations particular code carries out, and mark that code `{impl}`.\"\n\nThe assertions are substring checks on the real skill text, and they fail if either sentence is dropped or reworded. The guidance is bundled text, so a content check is the right kind of test.\n\n**Possible gaps I considered and rejected:**\n- The requirement's example, \"a convention every validation function follows\", is only an illustration (\"such as\"), so it needs no assertion.\n- The test checks only the habeas skill's reference, not every bundled skill. That skill is the home of the topic, and other tests (`bundled_skills_refer_to_a_topic_home_instead_of_restating_it` and `bundled_skills_explain_distributed_requirements`) check that the other skills refer to it.\n- The test is marked `{test}` for the subject, so there is no marking gap.",
  "references": "78662a5f93bdc1cce2c30f2a56821845f344b48e61610e0248463e30f52ffe47",
